fin-market-rules:ReferencePriceSpecification a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "ReferencePriceSpecification, is a versioned provenanced specification of the reference price used by a price-limit or circuit-breaker rule, used for making the price limit computable. It carries the price source, the observation window, the missing-value policy, the quote currency, and the rounding convention applied to the reference price before the band is computed, so that a limit up/down can be derived as reference price times the band ratio rounded to the tick without ambiguity.";
    rdfs:label "Reference Price Specification";
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r_1b3844897168dfaeb0f91e18, _:r_1e81c0575cdcd5e61d940ac2, _:r_2d9e93634bc2973e88651315, _:r_403dd219ceffc434401b4ab5, _:r_4b935a3681adeea2cd3b4e9c, _:r_75a1355648c69cfa3862ff0f, _:r_8d711db1bb3ccac743b2d187, _:r_8e76955c81e89653a392b6e7, _:r_b4d2bf93bb63ab3a39bfcf0d, _:r_d591baa89fd92214ba4d76b3, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactVersion>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/ProvenancedFact>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/TemporalFact>.
