fin-market-rules:RuleClause a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Rule Clause, is the abstract ordered executable clause superclass belonging to one exact market-rule version, used for carrying the concrete executable semantics of a rule. Concrete clause families specialize this class: range clauses carry an input interval with explicit boundaries and endpoint inclusivity and check ordering completeness against the rule's gap policy; trigger, date, and entitlement clauses carry their own typed semantics without requiring an input range. The bound and inclusivity attributes are optional here and apply only to range-bearing clauses.";
    rdfs:label "Rule Clause";
